Here is how you can create a string parameter with a default value in Go:

```go
func greet(name string) {
    if name == "" {
        name = "Guest"
    }
    fmt.Println("Hello, " + name)
}
```

Alternatively, you can use a pointer to a string to indicate whether a value was explicitly passed:

```go
func greet(name *string) {
    if name == nil {
        name = new(string)
        *name = "Guest"
    }
    fmt.Println("Hello, " + *name)
}
```

Or, using a custom type with a default value (Go 1.18+):

```go
type Greeting struct {
    Name string
}

func (g *Greeting) SetDefault() {
    if g.Name == "" {
        g.Name = "Guest"
    }
}
```

The first approach (checking for an empty string) is the most common and idiomatic way to handle default values for string parameters in Go.

